327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134923 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ee0b43b0-12d5-5c01-8688-826ce3b9f64c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134923 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134925 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134925 #edb/ref 1061 44504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134925 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d7f17594-7a91-5ca2-ae80-e61118138f81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134925 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135156 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's evaluate the triple integral\n\n![](images/ae/aec90ae0e9463c8e7c9164ed980828389070a8bb4a4ded54e2586f6c5a5ea376.svg)\n\nwhere the region ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/3e/3ee0df491365ac117eef84055f9d14aff9e7e5073b69e8e48b0a8bb93bb2f7ee.png)\n\n \n\nThe region ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) is a type II region. So, our first task is to fully describe this region.\n\nWe start by drawing an arrow parallel to the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis that \n\n- enters the region through the *back* surface ![](images/89/89c97ad93c125fc2b6f61d44fe9a90845fd289329d79d506c857f970d7586540.svg) and\n\n- leaves the region through the *front* surface ![](images/7b/7b823cb4664e2fe98090b6a778eba3030abf589930d2526ef5a50fb0aa792b5f.svg)\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/e6/e63827168c78ff5d13898bc436e02f99d834fbd2a10ce43aa98f47001e35044d.png)\n\n \n\nSo, our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n![](images/c4/c4a007ae116844babbe81721267c0526be0ee44b8b8007a799031eae12485a59.svg)\n\nwhere\n\n![](images/12/12d667e2c74a83bd8f7fe58be763862fc793d22774695995b56ccda713308381.svg)\n\nis the projection of ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) onto the ![](images/3f/3f84f2f8778b7916a5ee013c8a92440e5cbd510ba2768435c3139b45806d2f90.svg)-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/ea/ea267107ec908087a99eaea952caabb0d1a08488657b2c0f70a2502bbf4b869b.png)\n\nTo evaluate our triple integral, we start by expressing it as a mixed integral:\n\n![](images/13/13957704101661a7e52fa89ed897918c142fd1725742cf7b082d72eb54672e66.svg)\n\nNow, since the region ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) is a type I plane region, we can express the region ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) as\n\n![](images/53/535700690396dd4444e6f79015a447900af741cf14001fc2c552224e597a948b.svg)\n\nand therefore, our mixed integral can be written as the following repeated integral:\n\n![](images/68/6843abfc93fe5ae9a8f91fd2aaae7c725722ea8349021fb87430ddee5a51b9e2.svg)\n\nEvaluating this using the usual methods, we get\n\n![](images/3f/3f3fe0404f0c16535a37c7a739dd9f00cdc1b37dcfd076606cd57cd15063aabc.svg)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n![](images/07/07882d044aec2af88f6cc3c3282eadae112f1080bd8d5dc23667a7dcafcf3e1e.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135156 #edb/ref 1065 7132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135156 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0b832b39-a327-5109-b48b-d3097cb69ace" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135156 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135157 #edb/ref 1064 "When writing down a triple integral as a repeated integral, we can often skip the intermediate step of expressing our triple integral as a mixed integral.\n\nFor example, suppose we wish to evaluate\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R f(x,y,z)  \\: \\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region given by \n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: {\\color{red}a} \\leq y \\leq {\\color{red}b}, \\: {\\color{blue}v_1(y)} \\leq z \\leq {\\color{blue}v_2(y)}, \\: {\\color{purple}u_1(y,z)} \\leq x \\leq {\\color{purple}u_2(y,z)} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane is a type I plane region. Therefore, we can immediately express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z)\\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\int_{\\color{red}a}^{\\color{red}b} \\int_{\\color{blue}v_1(y)}^{\\color{blue}v_2(y)} \\int_{\\color{purple}u_1(y,z)}^{\\color{purple}u_2(y,z)} f(x,y,z)\\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135157 #edb/ref 1065 7133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135157 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "bcc6b25b-ebf4-5b46-9d69-4e4e068d107d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135157 #edb/ref 1067 "Skipping the Intermediate Step" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275550 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{14}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275550 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275550 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "085c1595-a112-5975-b0d5-4d9de18a8662" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275567 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275567 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275567 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0aa387c3-44ed-5bd4-9f84-186d277c7b83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275613 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{9}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275613 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275613 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0fbce1a0-73cf-5680-8b10-d475399b02ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275973 #edb/ref 1080 "42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275973 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275973 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "38384fb9-4559-5dfb-b210-72b9cc741634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276076 #edb/ref 1080 "90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276076 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276076 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "43967edf-f566-5b5c-8be1-4f953f652870" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276408 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276408 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175